+# Search Criteria
+
+- Scope: screen all 10 listings in the local packet and use only `housing/listings.csv` and the matching neighborhood notes as factual evidence.
+- Availability: the home must be available on or before 2026-10-15.
+- Space: require at least 2 bedrooms.
+- Pet: require dogs allowed.
+- Laundry: require in-unit laundry.
+- Corrected commute: require a peak-transit trip of no more than 35 minutes to Harbor Tech Campus.
+- Ranking and calculations: take exactly the three qualifying homes with the lowest recurring monthly total (monthly rent + parking + pet rent + estimated utilities), breaking ties by shorter grocery walk and then lower base rent; move-in cash is first month's rent + security deposit + one-time pet fee, and both cost figures are comparisons, not budget limits.
+
+# Shortlist
+
+| Rank | Home | Neighborhood | Bed / bath | Available | Commute | Recurring monthly total | Move-in cash | Outdoor space |
+|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Foundry House (L-106) | Foundry District | 2 / 1 | 2026-10-05 | 35 min to Harbor Tech Campus | $2,290 + $150 + $50 + $175 = $2,665 | $2,290 + $2,290 + $300 = $4,880 | Juliet balcony |
+| 2 | Juniper Place (L-109) | Juniper Hills | 2 / 2 | 2026-09-25 | 29 min to Harbor Tech Campus | $2,440 + $80 + $0 + $165 = $2,685 | $2,440 + $1,200 + $250 = $3,890 | private patio |
+| 3 | Beacon Flats (L-102) | Beacon North | 2 / 1.5 | 2026-10-10 | 31 min to Harbor Tech Campus | $2,380 + $120 + $35 + $160 = $2,695 | $2,380 + $1,800 + $350 = $4,530 | shared courtyard |
+
+# Trade-offs
+
+- Foundry House (L-106; Foundry District note) has the lowest recurring monthly total at $2,665, but its 35-minute trip sits exactly at the commute limit and its outdoor space is a Juliet balcony; the east-edge bedroom faces the rail corridor, where the note reports audible freight trains without indoor measurements.
+- Juniper Place (L-109; Juniper Hills note) costs only $20 more per month, shortens the commute to 29 minutes, has two bathrooms, and supplies a private patio; its 12-minute grocery walk returns steeply uphill for the final three blocks, and its parking is uncovered.
+- Beacon Flats (L-102; Beacon North note) is $30 per month above the primary option and has the highest move-in cash of the three, but it combines a 31-minute commute with the shortest grocery walk at four minutes and a shared courtyard; the note records late activity and street noise around Beacon Avenue, although the living room faces the courtyard.
+
+# Recommendation
+
+- Primary: choose Foundry House (L-106) for its first-place $2,665 recurring monthly total while retaining every space, pet, laundry, availability, and corrected commute requirement; accept that the commute has no buffer and the outdoor area is a Juliet balcony.
+- Runner-up: choose Juniper Place (L-109) if a private patio, second bathroom, six-minute commute buffer, and $990 lower move-in cash outweigh its $20 higher recurring monthly total, longer uphill grocery walk, and uncovered parking.
+- Before signing: reconfirm availability, fees, estimated utilities, pet terms, and peak transit timing from the packet, then inspect rail noise inside Foundry House and confirm that the Juliet balcony is adequate; the notes provide snapshots and visits, not guarantees or indoor sound measurements.
